The bounded C reduction tries split and joined LL/SC sequences at 128 stack
locations, with 100,000 attempts per location and a ten-second outer watchdog.
There is no competing thread. In the sealed ARM64 lane (same image identity as
floating-assembly.out), measured failed locations are:
                    split   joined
  GCC14 O0              6        0
  GCC14 O2              0        0
  Clang19 O0            0        0
  Clang19 O2            0        0
  EvoCC O2              8        0
All executions completed. These are measurements, not guaranteed counts on
another stack layout/CPU. The program's exit status checks only the joined
control; its printed split count is deliberately not concealed by exit zero.

Commands: reference -std=gnu11 -O0/-O2 source; subject --emit=asm
--target=aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu -std=gnu11 -O2 source, then GCC14 link.
Log and generated assembly:
.build/floating-targeted/strict-20260927/exclusive-window-*.

GCC's asm contract does not promise consecutive separate volatile statements:
https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc-14.2.0/gcc/Extended-Asm.html#AssemblerTemplate
Arm's exclusive-loop forward-progress conditions exclude intervening explicit
memory effects, including compiler-generated accesses:
https://documentation-service.arm.com/static/644c18cbaa78c007af74fa2c?token=
GCC PR92692 likewise keeps its own atomic operations bundled until after
prologue/epilogue generation; that fix is not an authorization to interpret or
combine arbitrary opaque asm strings in EvoCC:
https://gcc.gnu.org/legacy-ml/gcc-bugs/2020-01/msg02988.html

The identified lowering issue is independent of recognizing instructions:
every register output formerly forced addressable storage, even for an
unqualified automatic scalar with no address use. New SSA-result binding uses
the existing ordinary-local contract instead. Memory constraints, volatile,
addressed and aggregate objects retain their existing storage and writebacks.
The original CLI SSA-shape RED is captured in asm-output-ssa-red.log. The
first repaired lower-crate run passes 376 tests, including both optimization
modes and selected goto-edge binding. Native and original-program closure of
this additional repair is recorded below; scalar w support is separately GREEN.

